-- ============================================================================
-- H2 EXPERT DEEP SEED: Occupational Hygiene: Noise, Chemical & Heat Exposure,
-- advanced tier.
--
-- Six modules, 26 lessons, 132 questions (15 per module bank plus a 42
-- question final exam). The structure row is GENERATED from the tier's
-- manifest.json rather than hand typed, and the question rows from the
-- committed bank JSONs under tools/course-banks/hygiene/advanced.
--
-- What this tier owns: HEAT STRESS, THE LONG SHIFT, AND READING THE EVIDENCE.
-- The wet bulb globe temperature indoors and outdoors and the one-hour time
-- weighted averages of NIOSH 2016-106 sections 1.1.1 and 1.1.3; metabolic
-- rate in watts and the NIOSH heat RAL and REL equations, presented as
-- published equations CHECKED FOR TRANSCRIPTION ONLY; how strong the evidence
-- behind each formula in this course is, published against oracle only
-- against transcription; the published errata, including the NIOSH worked
-- example that disagrees with the NIOSH equation beside it; the shift that is
-- not eight hours, where the OSHA action level moves with the shift length
-- while the permissible exposure limit does not and the noise dose is summed
-- whole with no rescaling; the Brief and Scala daily and weekly reduction
-- factors and which of the two governs; and combining noise, chemical and
-- heat exposures into a sampling decision. Digest sections 16 to 23, and
-- section 24.
--
-- THE TRAP THE TIER IS BUILT ON. A long shift moves the trigger and not the
-- limit, and an adjusted limit can turn a mixture that passes into one that
-- fails without a single concentration changing. The Expert capstone grades
-- the two one-hour averages of STATED readouts, the extended-shift action
-- level, the whole-shift noise dose, one Brief and Scala adjusted limit and
-- the mixture index against the adjusted limits. It grades no NIOSH heat RAL,
-- no NIOSH heat REL, no margin against either, no exceedance verdict and no
-- wet bulb globe temperature built from thermometer readings: those are
-- taught as transcription-checked equations and graded nowhere.
-- ============================================================================

